window.__F=window.__F||{};window.__F["acc-03.html"]="<div class=\"ac-info\"><p class=\"ac-i-main\">تشخيص مضخّم Premium 3. يُعرَف بكود المبيعات: RCA هارمن كاردون (19 سماعة)، وRGE نظام صوت بريميوم (18 سماعة).</p><p class=\"ac-i-tip\"><b>متى تستعمله:</b> الأكواد لقنوات السماعات 1 إلى 19 تقريباً: قصر أو قطع أو أداء. حدّد أولاً كود المبيعات ثم اتبع الخطوات.</p><div class=\"ac-chips\"><span class=\"en-chip\">B = كهرباء الجسم: 65</span><span class=\"en-chip\">U = اتصال الشبكة: 5</span></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong>كيف تقرأ كود العطل</strong><small>الرقم بعد الشرطة يدل على نوع العطل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"ac-legend\"><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-11</b><span>قصر على الأرضي</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-12</b><span>قصر على البطارية</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-13</b><span>دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-15</b><span>قصر على البطارية أو دائرة مفتوحة</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-16</b><span>الفولتية أقل من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-17</b><span>الفولتية أعلى من الحد</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-2A</b><span>مفتاح عالق Stuck</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-84 / 85</b><span>الإشارة أقل / أعلى من المدى</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-92</b><span>أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</span></div><div><b dir=\"ltr\">-00</b><span>عطل عام أو بدون نوع محدد</span></div></div><p class=\"bcm-note\">الحرف الأول: B = كهرباء الجسم · C = الهيكل والحساسات · P = نقل الحركة · U = اتصال الشبكة. نفّذ دائماً الفحص المسبق Pre-Diagnostic قبل خطوات أي كود.</p></div></details></div><input type=\"search\" class=\"ec-search acc-q\" placeholder=\"ابحث: كود العطل أو كلمة من الوصف\" aria-label=\"بحث\"><p class=\"bcm-note acc-cnt\">70 كود عطل. اضغط على الكود لترى شرحه.</p><div class=\"acc-list\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1460-11 channel 1 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1460-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 1 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:      The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE LEFT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ensure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Instrument Panel Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X209) AMPLIFIED LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X299) AMPLIFIED LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1460-12 channel 1 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1460-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 1 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:      The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X209) LEFT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Amplified Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X299) LEFT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1460-13 channel 1 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1460-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 1 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                     SALES CODE                                     DESCRIPTION\n    RCA                                               19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\n    RGE                                               18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT FRONT I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and set the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Amplified Left I/P Speaker circuits in the Amplified Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified Left I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X209) LEFT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X299) LEFT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1460-92 channel 1 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1460-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 1 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel, when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1464-00 channel 1 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1464-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 1 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE AMPLIFIED</li><li>LEFT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>LEFT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the speaker between the two speaker terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X209) AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X299) AMPLIFIED LEFT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X209) Left I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to the (X299) Left I/P Speaker (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1465-11 channel 2 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1465-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 2 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RIGHT INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Instrument Panel Speaker in accordance with the Service Information.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X208) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X208) Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the(X208) Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X208) Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X298) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1465-12 channel 2 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1465-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 2 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record them on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X208) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Amplified Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X298) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1465-13 channel 2 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1465-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 2 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT FRONT I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Amplified Right I/P Speaker circuits at the Amplified Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified Right I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X208) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit between the</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Amplified Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X298) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Amplified Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1465-92 channel 2 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1465-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 2 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For a complete wiring diagram, refer to appropriate SYSTEM WIRING DIAGRAMS article .</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel, when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the service information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1469-00 channel 2 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1469-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 2 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P</li><li>SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RESISTANCE OF THE AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplified Right I/P Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the speaker between the two speaker terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified Right I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X208) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X298) AMPLIFIED RIGHT I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X208) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X298) Amplified Right I/P Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146a-11 channel 3 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146A-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 3 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Left Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X201) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X291) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146a-12 channel 3 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146A-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 3 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X201) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X291) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146a-13 channel 3 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146A-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 3 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Left Front Door Speaker circuits in the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X201) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X291) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146a-92 channel 3 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146A-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 3 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146e-00 channel 3 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146E-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 3 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>(-) CIRCUIT</li><li>LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the speaker between the two terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X201) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X291) LEFT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X201) Left Front Door Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X291) Left Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146f-11 channel 4 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146F-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 4 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Right Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X202) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X292) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146f-12 channel 4 audio speaker output-circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146F-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 4 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT-CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X202) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X292) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146f-13 channel 4 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146F-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 4 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Right Front Door Speaker circuits in the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X202) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X292) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Front Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b146f-92 channel 4 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B146F-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 4 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects that the output circuits are shorted together when the ignition is cycled on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE RIGHT FRONT DOOR</li><li>SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record them on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Front Door Speaker.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) terminal and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) terminal at the Speaker connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Front Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X202) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X292) RIGHT FRONT DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X202) Right Front Door Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X292) Right Front Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1474-11 channel 5 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1474-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 5 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Ensure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER 1 (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPAEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit ?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1474-12 channel 5 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1474-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 5 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER 1 (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit and ground at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPAEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit and ground at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1474-13 channel 5 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1474-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 5 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record them on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a Voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Left Rear Speaker circuits at the Amplified Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1 Volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified Left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER 1 (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Amplified Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPAEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Amplified Left Rearr Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1474-92 channel 5 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1474-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 5 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel, when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1478-00 channel 5 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1478-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 5 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier (AMP) DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record them on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR A SHORTED LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the speaker between the two Speaker terminals.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER 1 (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier harness C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1479-11 channel 6 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1479-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 6 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CENTER I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE CENTER (I/P) SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Center (I/P) Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Center (I/P) Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X200) CENTER (I/P) SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X200) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X200) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X200) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X290) CENTER (I/P) SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X290) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X290) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X290) Center Instrument Panel (I/P) Speaker (-) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1479-12 channel 6 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1479-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 6 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X200) CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Amplified Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X290) CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1479-13 channel 6 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1479-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 6 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects an open condition on the speaker output circuit.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>CENTER I/P SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE CENTER FRONT I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the radio on and set the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Amplified Center I/P Speaker circuits in the Amplified Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplified Center I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X200) CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">harness connector and the Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X290) CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1479-92 channel 6 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1479-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 6 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel When the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b147d-00 channel 6 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B147D-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 6 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:   The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED CENTER INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE AMPLIFIED</li><li>CENTER INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>CENTER INSTRUMENT PANEL (I/P) SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the front and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Center I/P Speaker C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplified Center I/P Speaker connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Center I/P Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X200) AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X290) AMPLIFIED CENTER I/P SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit and the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (X200) Center I/P Speaker (+) circuit for a short to the (X290) Center I/P Speaker (-) circuit.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b147e-11 channel 7 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B147E-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 7 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:        The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Subwoofer Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X300) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X390) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b147e-12 channel 7 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B147E-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 7 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X300) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1(+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X390) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit at the</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Amplifier C2 harness connector</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b147e-13 channel 7 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B147E-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 7 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Subwoofer Speaker circuits in the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Subwoofer Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X300) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X390) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b147e-92 channel 7 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B147E-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 7 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the speaker input circuit when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1482-00 channel 7 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1482-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 7 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the Subwoofer output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE SUBWOOFER SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Subwoofer Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit, and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuit at the Subwoofer.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Subwoofer Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X300) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X390) AMPLIFIED SUBWOOFER 1 (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit, and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuits at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Is there continuity between the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuits?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair the (X300) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (+) circuit, and the (X390) Amplified Subwoofer 1 (-) circuits for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1483-11 channel 8 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1483-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 8 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X206) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X296) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1483-12 channel 8 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1483-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 8 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X206) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X296) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1483-13 channel 8 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1483-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 8 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Test complete, the condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Right Rear Door Speaker circuits at the Right Rear Door Speaker connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X206) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X296) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1483-92 channel 8 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1483-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 8 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel, when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1487-00 channel 8 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1487-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 8 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>(-) CIRCUIT</li><li>RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Right Rear Door Speaker.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X206) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X296) RIGHT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X296) Right</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X206) Right Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X296) Right Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b1488-00 cabin eq mismatch performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B1488-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CABIN EQ MISMATCH PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">BCM active on the bus.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">If the Cabin Equalization Curve number message from the Radio is not the same as the Cabin Equalization Curve number stored in the Amplifier for 10 consecutive cycles, then the Radio will set this DTC.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>NO COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE (BCM)</li><li>ACTIVE BCM DTCs</li><li>RADIO</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase Radio DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read Radio DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK RADIO BUSSED INPUTS/SENSORS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool in Radio Data Display, read the Cabin Equalization Curve number in the Bussed Inputs and Sensors Sections.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The Cabin EQ Curve settings in the Inputs/Sensors section should match one another. The Cabin EQ# in the Inputs section is the information that is received from the BCM. The Cabin EQ in the Sensors section is the information that is Stored in the Amplifier&#x27;s memory.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Do the Cabin EQ settings match one another?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Radio in accordance to the service information. Refer to RADIO, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>VERIFY COMMUNICATION WITH AMPLIFIER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active modules on the BUS.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the scan tool show the Amplifier active on the BUS?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the No Response From the Amplifier diagnostic procedure. Refer to NO RESPONSE FROM AMP (AMPLIFIER) .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE AMPLIFIER FOR ACTIVE DTCs</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, erase Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Turn the ignition off. Wait approximately 10 seconds.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are any active DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure. Refer to DTC INDEX .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Radio in accordance to the service information. Refer to RADIO, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14b9-11 channel 9 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14B9-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 9 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14b9-12 channel 9 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14B9-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 9 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14b9-13 channel 9 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14B9-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 9 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Left Rear Speaker circuits at the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14b9-2b channel 9 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14B9-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 9 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the speaker output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR</li><li>SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Left rear Speaker.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X303) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X393) AMPLIFIED LEFT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X393)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X303) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X393) Amplified Left Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14b9-92 channel 9 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14B9-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 9 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel When the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14be-11 channel 10 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14BE-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 10 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Shelf Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X394) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit ?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14be-12 channel 10 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14BE-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 10 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X304) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X394) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14be-13 channel 10 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14BE-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 10 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier (AMP) DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Right Rear Shelf Speaker circuits at the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Shelf Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C1 harness connector and the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X394) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C1 harness connector and the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14be-2b channel 10 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14BE-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 10 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE RIGHT REAR SHELF</li><li>SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit at the Right Rear Shelf Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right rear Shelf Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X394) RIGHT REAR SHELF SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C1 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X304) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394) Right Rear Shelf Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14be-92 channel 10 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14BE-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 10 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the speaker output circuit when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b143c-11 channel 11 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B143C-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 11 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read the active Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X205) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X295) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b143c-12 channel 11 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B143C-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 11 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X205) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X295) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b143c-13 channel 11 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B143C-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 11 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the Radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a Voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Left Rear Door Speaker circuits in the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 Volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X205) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">harness connector and the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X295) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance below 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b143c-2b channel 11 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B143C-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 11 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-)</li><li>CIRCUIT</li><li>LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE LEFT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Left Rear Door Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit terminals at the Left rear Door Speaker.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Left Rear Door Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X205) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X295) LEFT REAR DOOR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X205) Left Rear Door Speaker (+) circuit, and the (X295) Left Rear Door Speaker (-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c3-92 channel 11 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C3-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 11 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel, when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c8-11 channel 12 audio speaker output - circuit short to ground\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C8-11</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 12 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO GROUND</small><small>العطل: قصر على الأرضي</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                 19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                 18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects a shorted to ground condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Make sure one of the front doors is still open.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase the DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X394) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR A SHORT TO GROUND</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Check for continuity between ground and the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between ground and the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to ground.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c8-12 channel 12 audio speaker output - circuit short to battery\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C8-12</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 12 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORT TO BATTERY</small><small>العطل: قصر على البطارية</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects a short to battery condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO VOLTAGE</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X304) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X304) Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK FOR VOLTAGE ON THE (X394) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the voltage between ground and the (X394) Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there any voltage present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit for a short to voltage.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c8-13 channel 12 audio speaker output - circuit open\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C8-13</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 12 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT OPEN</small><small>العطل: دائرة مفتوحة</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">audio system configurations noted below.</p><pre class=\"en-pre\">                 SALES CODE                                      DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects an open condition on the speaker output circuits.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT OPEN</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:            A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Turn the radio on and turn the volume to 25.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With a voltmeter set to read in A/C voltage, measure the voltage of the Right Rear Speaker circuits in the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the voltage present greater than 1.0 volt?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (X394) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Measure the resistance of the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit between the Amplifier C2 harness connector and the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance above 3.0 Ohms?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit for an open.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c8-2b channel 12 audio speaker output - circuit shorted together\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C8-2B</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 12 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - CIRCUIT SHORTED TOGETHER</small><small>العطل: قصر بين الدوائر</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">NO TITLE</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:     The use of speaker channel mapping and sales codes are being used to quickly identify those differences in location; and the total number of speakers in the audio system configurations noted below.</div><pre class=\"en-pre\">                  SALES CODE                                       DESCRIPTION\nRCA                                                  19 HARMAN KARDON GREENEDGE SPKRS\nRGE                                                  18 SPEAKERS PREMIUM AUDIO SYSTEM</pre></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier detects that the output circuits are shorted together.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT SHORTED TO THE AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR</li><li>SPEAKER (-) CIRCUIT</li><li>AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK THE OPERATION OF THE AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Right Rear Speaker harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Measure the resistance between the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Right Rear Speaker.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the resistance of the speaker less than 1.0 Ohm?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Right Rear Speaker in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to SPEAKER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (X304) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (+) CIRCUIT, AND THE (X394) AMPLIFIED RIGHT REAR SPEAKER (-) CIRCUITS FOR A SHORT TOGETHER</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Check for continuity between the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is there continuity between the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394)</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Amplified Right Rear Speaker (-) circuit?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Repair the (X304) Amplified Right Rear Speaker (+) circuit and the (X394) Amplified Right Rear Speaker(-) circuit for a short together.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b14c8-92 channel 12 audio speaker output - performance or incorrect\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B14C8-92</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CHANNEL 12 AUDIO SPEAKER OUTPUT - PERFORMANCE OR INCORRECT</small><small>العطل: أداء ضعيف أو تشغيل غير صحيح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">OPERATION</p></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) sets if a Direct Current (DC) offset occurs on the output channel when the ignition is cycled on. The Amplifier shall set a DTC after a maturity rate of four to six seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition on and open one of the front doors.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:             A front door must remain open whenever checking or erasing Amplifier DTCs.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Cycle the ignition switch from on to off, wait five seconds and then back to on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Turn the Radio on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>Adjust the speakers to the rear and center.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-16 battery voltage - circuit voltage below threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-16</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE BELOW THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أقل من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier monitors the input voltage. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set when the input voltage is below 9 volts for greater than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT OPEN OR EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE</li><li>GROUND CIRCUIT OPEN OR EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE</li><li>CHARGING SYSTEM CONCERN</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Make sure the battery is fully charged before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PCM DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Allow the engine to idle for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>CHECK THE (A931) FUSED B(+) CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          Check the AMPLIFIER fuse for an open. If the fuse is open, make sure to check for a short to ground prior to replacing the fuse.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Turn the ignition off.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Turn the ignition on.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to ground, check the (A931) Fused B(+) circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The test light must illuminate brightly. Compare the brightness to that of a direct connection to the battery.</div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 4</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (A931) Fused B(+) circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>CHECK THE (Z911) GROUND CIRCUIT FOR AN OPEN OR EXCESSIVE RESISTANCE</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With a 12-volt test light connected to 12 volts, check the (Z911) Ground circuit at the Amplifier C2 harness connector.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Does the test light illuminate brightly?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair the (Z911) Ground circuit for an open or high resistance.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b2199-17 battery voltage - circuit voltage above threshold\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B2199-17</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">BATTERY VOLTAGE - CIRCUIT VOLTAGE ABOVE THRESHOLD</small><small>العطل: فولتية الدائرة أعلى من الحد</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier monitors the input voltage. This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set when the input voltage is above 16 volts for greater than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CHARGING SYSTEM CONCERN</li><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCS</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read the PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, read Amplifier DTCs and record on the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Start the engine.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Allow the engine to idle for two minutes.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>With the scan tool, read the Amplifier DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the DTC active?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The condition or conditions that originally set this DTC are not present at this time. Using the wiring diagrams as a guide, check all related splices and connectors for signs of water intrusion, corrosion, pushed out or bent terminals, and correct pin tension. If no problems are found, test complete.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-84 system voltage - signal below allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-84</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL BELOW ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أقل من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set when the Amplifier receives a CAN message indicating the battery voltage is below 10 volts for greater than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>LOW SYSTEM VOLTAGE</li><li>BATTERY OR CHARGING SYSTEM</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           Make sure the battery is fully charged before proceeding.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read the active PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This DTC is informational only. At some time there was a low battery system voltage. Check the battery and charging system in accordance with the Service Information.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b21dd-85 system voltage - signal above allowable range\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B21DD-85</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">SYSTEM VOLTAGE - SIGNAL ABOVE ALLOWABLE RANGE</small><small>العطل: الإشارة أعلى من المدى المسموح</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This Diagnostic Trouble Code (DTC) is set when the Amplifier receives a CAN message indicating the battery voltage is above 16 volts for greater than 15 seconds.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>HIGH BATTERY SYSTEM VOLTAGE</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CHECK FOR POWERTRAIN CONTROL MODULE (PCM) DTCs</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Using the scan tool, read the active PCM DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Are there any battery or charging system DTCs present?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Refer to DTC INDEX and perform the appropriate diagnostic procedure.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">This DTC is informational only. At some time there was a high battery system voltage. Check the charging system in accordance with the Service Information.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"b221f-00 amplifier internal\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">B221F-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">AMPLIFIER INTERNAL</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier has constant fused B+ feed and ground to the module. When an ignition on command is sent over the CAN bus, the Amplifier will wake up and turn on. The Amplifier receives the audio signal circuits from the radio&#x27;s front right and left, and rear right and left audio inputs and then converts the signals to amplified audio signals to the speakers. The Amplifier monitors the speaker output feeds for any speaker concerns, wiring opens or shorts.</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following condition is met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The Amplifier (AMP) detects an internal failure.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الإجراء الافتراضي · <span dir=\"ltr\">Default Action</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Power IC automatically shuts down individual channel speaker output when this fault is detected.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>AMPLIFIER</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">REPLACE THE RADIO AMPLIFIER</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>When this DTC is active, replace the Amplifier.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Replace the Amplifier in accordance with the Service Information. Refer to AMPLIFIER, REMOVAL .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0010-00 can interior bus\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0010-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN INTERIOR BUS</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN system operation, Refer to DTC INDEX</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition is on. Battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">Voltage on the CAN IHS bus is outside of a calibrated range.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT OPEN OR HIGH RESISTANCE</li><li>CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT SHORTED TO GROUND</li><li>CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT SHORTED TO ANOTHER CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED ECU</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED STAR CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED SPLICE BLOCK CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>ATTEMPT TO DUPLICATE THE CONDITION</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           This DTC sets when the CAN IHS bus is disabled. If the scan tool is able to read this DTC, then the fault is currently NOT active. This diagnostic procedure only troubleshoots an intermittent condition. Follow this procedure to attempt to locate the intermittent condition or induce the fault so the diagnostic procedures under SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS can be followed. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Is the fault now present?</p><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           If the fault is present, the scan tool will not communicate with modules on the CAN IHS bus.</div><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:          The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN IHS bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN IHS bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN IHS circuits at each related module, in-line connector, and Star/Splice Block Connector (if equipped) while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform repairs as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN IHS related modules harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions:</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Other signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Reconnect all CAN IHS related modules harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Reconnect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, attempt to communicate with the CAN IHS bus.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Does the scan tool communicate with the CAN IHS bus?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0011-00 can interior bus off performance\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0011-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">CAN INTERIOR BUS OFF PERFORMANCE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">THEORY OF OPERATION</strong><small>نظرية العمل</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">For an in-depth explanation of the CAN system operation, refer to DESCRIPTION .</p></div></div></details><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>متى يتحقق · <span dir=\"ltr\">When Monitored</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">This diagnostic runs continuously when the following conditions are met:</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">With the ignition on. Battery voltage is between 10.0 and 16.0 volts.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>شرط التسجيل · <span dir=\"ltr\">Set Condition</span></b><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">CAN IHS bus has experienced a failure due to a circuit or processor fault.</p></div></div><div class=\"ac-f\"><b>الأسباب المحتملة · <span dir=\"ltr\">Possible Causes</span></b><ul class=\"en-ul\" dir=\"ltr\"><li>OPEN OR SHORTED CAN IHS BUS CIRCUIT</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED MODULE</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED STAR CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>CAN IHS RELATED SPLICE BLOCK CONNECTOR (IF EQUIPPED)</li><li>Always perform the PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE before proceeding.</li><li>Refer to PRE-DIAGNOSTIC TROUBLESHOOTING PROCEDURE .</li></ul></div><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv3\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">DIAGNOSTIC TEST</strong><small>خطوات الفحص</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>CHECK FOR AN ACTIVE DTC</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         If the scan tool will not communicate with CAN IHS, proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, run a Vehicle Scan Report and attached it to the repair order.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Go To 2</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>ATTEMPT TO LOCATE AN INTERMITTENT CIRCUIT FAULT</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:         The scan tool LOSS OF COMM TEST will force the modules on the CAN IHS bus to continuously ping each other.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>With the scan tool, initiate the LOSS OF COMM TEST.</span></div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           A value above 0 under the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES can help indicate the location of a circuit fault while wiggling the related CAN IHS bus circuits.</div><div class=\"ct-note en-kw\">NOTE:           The scan tool lag time between pings is almost 1 full second. Keep this in mind while wiggling the wires and connectors.</div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>In a systematic manner, wiggle the applicable CAN IHS circuits at each related module, in-line</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">connector, and Star/Splice Block Connector (if equipped) while monitoring the NUMBER OF NO RESPONSES on the scan tool.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the above test help locate the fault?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Repair as necessary.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform the BODY VERIFICATION TEST. Refer to BODY VERIFICATION TEST .</p><p class=\"ac-yn no\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">لا · No</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Go To 3</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>PERFORM VISUAL INSPECTION OF CONNECTORS, TERMINALS AND WIRES</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">1</span><span>Disconnect all CAN IHS related module harness connectors.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">2</span><span>Disconnect all related in-line harness connections.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">3</span><span>Inspect the harness connectors, component connectors, and all male and female terminals for the following conditions: Proper connector installation. Damaged connector locks. Corrosion. Signs of water intrusion. Weather seal damage (if equipped). Bent terminals. Overheating due to a poor connection (terminal may be discolored due to excessive current draw). Terminals that have been pushed back into the connector cavity.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Perform a terminal drag test on each connector terminal to verify proper terminal tension.</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Repair any conditions that are found.</p><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">4</span><span>Connect all CAN IHS related module harness connectors. Be certain that all harness connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">5</span><span>Connect all in-line harness connectors. Be certain that all connectors are fully seated and the connector locks are fully engaged.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">6</span><span>With the scan tool, erase DTCs.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">7</span><span>Using the Vehicle Scan Report, along with the When Monitored and Set Conditions above, operate the vehicle in the conditions that set the DTC.</span></div><div class=\"en-step\" style=\"margin-inline-start:10px\"><span class=\"ec-no\">8</span><span>With the scan tool, read DTCs.</span></div><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">Did the DTC return?</p><p class=\"ac-yn yes\" style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">نعم · Yes</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:30px\">Proceed to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS. Refer to SCAN TOOL DOES NOT COMMUNICATE WITH CAN IHS .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:20px\">No The conditions that caused this DTC to set are no longer present. Test complete.</p></div></div></details></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0140-00 lost communication with body control module\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0140-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH BODY CONTROL MODULE</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع BODY CONTROL MODULE</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u0184-00 lost communication with radio\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U0184-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH RADIO</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع RADIO</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p></div></div></details><details class=\"pcm-component-details ct-d en-sec lv2 acc-dtc\" data-s=\"u11fb-00 lost communication with left blind spot sensor\"><summary><span class=\"ct-ttl\"><strong dir=\"ltr\">U11FB-00</strong><small dir=\"ltr\" style=\"opacity:.8\">LOST COMMUNICATION WITH LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR</small><small>فقد الاتصال مع LEFT BLIND SPOT SENSOR</small></span></summary><div class=\"ct-body\"><div class=\"en-raw\" dir=\"ltr\"><p style=\"margin-inline-start:0px\">The COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE MUST be performed before replacing any component(s) or module(s). Perform the COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE. Refer to COMMUNICATION DIAGNOSTIC PROCEDURE .</p><p style=\"margin-inline-start:40px\">Article GUID: A00910339</p></div></div></details></div>";
